  "slug": "batch-record-production-log-form",
  "title": "Batch Record Production Log Form",
  "subtitle": "Control the starting state, record chronological batch execution and production record control activity, reconcile quantities and holds, authorize restarts, and hand off the next due check.",
  "description": "A chronological batch record production log form for reconstructing how a manufacturing batch and its complete execution history moved through readiness, execution, interruptions, measurements, quantity reconciliation, exceptions, restart decisions, and shift closeout.",
  "use_case": "Use during active batch execution and production record control work when operators and reviewers need a time-ordered trace that identifies who did what, the actual result, affected range, and last known acceptable status.",
  "risk_tier": "A",
